.TH LIBRDP-COCOA-WORKSPACE 1 "2026-07-15" "librdp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-cocoa-workspace \- native macOS workspace feed launcher for librdp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-cocoa-workspace
.B --feed
.I url
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-cocoa-workspace
fetches an RDS workspace feed through the public workspace API, prints the published resources, and displays a Cocoa summary window unless
.B --no-window
is supplied. With
.B --launch
it starts the selected resource through a viewer executable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --feed " url"
Workspace feed URL.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
Feed user name.
.TP
.BI --password " value"
Feed password. Avoid placing credentials in shell history on shared systems.
.TP
.BI --password-env " name"
Read the feed password from an environment variable.
.TP
.BI --domain " name"
Authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --timeout " ms"
Feed timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.BI --select " id|index|title|alias"
Select a published resource. Required when the feed contains multiple resources and
.B --launch
is used.
.TP
.BI --viewer " path"
Viewer executable. The default is
.BR librdp-cocoa-viewer .
.TP
.BI --security " auto|rdp|tls|nla"
Security mode passed to the viewer.
.TP
.B --launch
Launch the selected resource.
.TP
.B --no-window
Run only as a command-line tool.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp-cocoa-viewer (1),
.BR librdp-workspace (7),
.BR librdp-api (7)
